# Secrets: never commit. This project needs NO RPC key -- forward logging reads the chain tip,
# which every free public endpoint serves -- so the only secrets are the data-repo deploy key and
# the storefront token, both of which live in GitHub Secrets and never on disk.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
credentials*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# The collected panels are pushed to the PRIVATE data repo, not committed here. This repo is
# public so that Actions minutes are free; publishing the code costs nothing, because a copier
# still starts accumulating from today while we already hold history.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
# The pre-registration ledger IS the record: its whole value is being timestamped and
# version-controlled, so it is force-tracked here exactly as Bot/.gitignore does. Same convention,
# same reason.
!data/experiments.csv

# Downloaded panel cache for src/research. Deliberately NOT under data/, because on a runner that
# path is the checked-out private data repo and the workflow runs `git add -A` inside it; a
# multi-hundred-MB cache landing there would bloat the repo toward the 5 GB ceiling that
# prune_git.py exists to hold off. Regenerable from HuggingFace, so losing it costs nothing.
.research_cache/

# Built products. `dist/` holds BOTH the free rolling sample and the FULL PAID SNAPSHOT. This
# repo is PUBLIC, so committing dist/ would publish the paid product and destroy the only thing
# being sold. Products are built fresh by src/ops/publish.py and uploaded to the storefront;
# they are never version-controlled here.
dist/

# Stale-window sentinel: written by hf_push inside Actions, consumed by the workflow.
.repin_needed
